The most effective GA improved the fitness function value from 68.26 (initial best chromosome) to 979.16 after 200 iterations, demonstrating the efficacy of the proposed approach. Furthermore, variations in specific hyperparameters, such as learning rate, gamma, and update frequency, were shown to substantially affect the DQN model’s learning ability.

